<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick II, Grand Duke of Baden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Friedrich II of Baden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick II was the last Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>, reigning from 1907 to 1918, the son of Frederick I and a grandson of Emperor William I. During the war he held a nominal army command. After a provisional government was formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karlsruhe">Karlsruhe</a> in November 1918 he abdicated, and Baden became a democratic republic within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-grand-duke-of-baden.jpg" alt="Frederick II, Grand Duke of Baden" width="309" height="500" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Th. Schumann &amp; Son, Karlsruhe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:II._Frigyes_badeni_nagyherceg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
